// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//   DONKEY KONG (1981) — Full Arcade Recreation
//   A play-by-play recreation of Nintendo's 1981 arcade classic,
//   built on perchance.org with vanilla JS + canvas.
//
//   ROADMAP: generated with the atomic-roadmap method
//   (see scratch/roadmap.md) — see roadmap comment block below.
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// 
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//   ROADMAP — atomic task backlog (atomic-roadmap method)
//   Check off tasks with [x] as they are completed.
//   66 tasks · 10 phases · generated for the Perchance AI Helper
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// 
// ## Phase 1: Framework & Branding
// 1. [x] **Bootstrap Project Structure**: Create `main.pjs` for state/config and `index.html` for layout; initialize a canvas 2D context with a fixed 224x256 resolution scaled to fit window.
// 2. [x] **Render Loop**: Implement a `requestAnimationFrame` loop in `src/game.js` that clears the canvas to `#000033` (dark blue) and logs "Frame Rendered" to console.
// 3. [x] **Roadmap Checklist**: Implement a hidden debug UI in `index.html` that lists all roadmap tasks, allowing the agent to mark them complete via `localStorage`.
// 4. [x] **Input Manager**: Create a keyboard listener mapping `ArrowLeft`, `ArrowRight`, `ArrowUp`, `ArrowDown`, and `Space` (Jump) to a `keys` state object.
// 5. [x] **Visual Test Harness**: Draw a 16x16 red square (Player proxy) and a 16x16 blue rectangle (Platform proxy) to verify coordinates and rendering scale.
// 
// ## Phase 2: Core Physics & Player Movement
// 6. [x] **Player State Machine**: Implement `Player` class with states: `IDLE`, `WALKING`, `CLIMBING`, `JUMPING`, `DYING`.
// 7. [x] **Horizontal Movement**: Implement left/right movement with acceleration/friction and collision detection against canvas edges.
// 8. [x] **Gravity & Jumping**: Implement a jump arc using a vertical velocity variable; verify Mario can jump and land on a static platform.
// 9. [x] **Ladder Logic**: Implement "Ladder Zones" where `ArrowUp`/`ArrowDown` allows the player to transition between vertical levels.
// 10. [x] **Ladder Edge Grabbing**: Implement logic to snap the player to the top of a ladder if they overlap the top edge while falling.
// 11. [x] **Fall Logic**: Implement "hole" detection in platforms (ladders) allowing the player to fall through to the level below.
// 
// ## Phase 3: Screen 1 Architecture (25m)
// 12. [x] **Girder Layout**: Define a data array for Screen 1: 5 girders with specific x/y coordinates and slight clockwise rotations (slopes).
// 13. [x] **Procedural Girders**: Render girders as cyan lines (`#00FFFF`) with small grey circles for rivets.
// 14. [x] **Ladder Rendering**: Render ladders as sets of parallel vertical lines connecting the girders.
// 15. [x] **Barrel Spawner**: Implement a `Barrel` class and a spawner at the top-left (Donkey Kong's position) that pushes barrels into a queue.
// 16. [x] **Barrel Physics**: Implement barrel rolling: move horizontally, detect girder collisions, and "fall" through ladder gaps.
// 17. [x] **Ramp Deflection**: Implement logic where barrels hitting a sloped girder change direction to roll down to the next level.
// 18. [x] **Barrel-Player Collision**: Implement a hitbox check; if player touches barrel without Hammer, trigger `DYING` state.
// 
// ## Phase 4: Items, Power-ups & Scoring
// 19. [x] **Score HUD**: Create a top-bar UI showing `SCORE`, `HI-SCORE`, and `LIVES` (initialized to 3).
// 20. [x] **Collectibles**: Spawn the Hat, Handbag, and Parasol at fixed coordinates on Screen 1; implement collision and point addition.
// 21. [x] **Hammer Power-up**: Implement a Hammer spawn timer; when collected, player state changes to `HAMMER_MODE` for 5 seconds.
// 22. [x] **Hammer Combat**: In `HAMMER_MODE`, player can destroy barrels on contact (500 pts) instead of dying.
// 23. [x] **Jump Scoring**: Implement logic to award 100 points when a barrel's X-position is passed by a jumping player.
// 24. [x] **Pauline & Win Condition**: Place Pauline at the top; colliding with her triggers "Level Clear" and 5000 points.
// 
// ## Phase 5: Fireballs & Hazards
// 25. [x] **Fireball Spawner**: Implement a spawner at the oil cans on Screen 1.
// 26. [x] **Fireball AI**: Fireballs move horizontally, climb ladders randomly, and patrol girders.
// 27. [x] **Fireball Evolution**: Implement a timer where fireballs turn blue (increased speed/points) after a set duration.
// 28. [x] **Fireball Collision**: Implement death trigger upon contact with fireballs.
// 
// ## Phase 6: Screen 2 - Conveyor Belts
// 29. [x] **Conveyor belt logic**: Implement movement modifiers that push the player left or right based on belt direction.
// 30. [x] **Screen 2 layout**: Define the platform and belt positions for the 50m mark.
// 31. [x] **Barrel spawning**: Implement barrel spawners specific to Screen 2.
// 32. [x] **Collision refinement**: Ensure player/barrel interactions remain consistent on moving belts.
// 33. [x] **Screen transition**: Implement the trigger to move from Screen 1 to Screen 2.
// 34. [x] **Screen 2 win condition**: Define the trigger to advance to Screen 3.
// 
// ## Phase 7: Screen 3 - Elevators & Oil
// 35. [x] **Elevator base class**: Create a system for platforms that move vertically between two set points.
// 36. [x] **Blue elevators**: Implement platforms that move up/down on a set timer.
// 37. [x] **Pink elevators**: Implement platforms that move up/down with a different timing/offset.
// 38. [x] **Player riding logic**: Ensure player stays pinned to the platform while it moves.
// 39. [x] **Oil can fire**: Implement fire hazard entities at the bottom of the screen.
// 40. [x] **Item spawning**: Place collectable items throughout the elevator shafts.
// 41. [x] **Item collection logic**: Implement score increase and visual feedback for collected items.
// 42. [x] **Screen 3 layout**: Finalize the spatial arrangement of elevators and hazards.
// 43. [x] **Screen transition**: Implement the trigger to move from Screen 2 to Screen 3.
// 
// ## Phase 8: Screen 4 - The Rivets
// 44. [x] **Rivet entity**: Create a "Rivet" object that can be toggled between active and removed.
// 45. [x] **Rivet trigger**: Implement logic where stepping on a rivet removes it from the game world.
// 46. [x] **Rivet tracking**: Create a counter to track how many rivets remain on the screen.
// 47. [x] **Structure collapse logic**: Implement a "collapse" state that triggers when all rivets are removed.
// 48. [x] **Collapse animation**: Create a visual sequence where the platforms fall away.
// 49. [x] **Screen 4 layout**: Design the rivet-based structure.
// 50. [x] **Level Win trigger**: Implement the final victory state upon structure collapse.
// 51. [x] **Screen transition**: Implement the trigger to move from Screen 3 to Screen 4.
// 
// ## Phase 9: Game Flow & UI
// 52. [x] **Title Screen**: Create the main menu with "Start Game" and "Instructions".
// 53. [x] **Game State Manager**: Implement transitions between Title -> Gameplay -> Game Over -> Victory.
// 54. [x] **2-Player Setup**: Add logic for a second player (input mapping and spawn).
// 55. [x] **Player 2 collisions**: Ensure P2 interacts correctly with all screen mechanics.
// 56. [x] **Lives/Score System**: Implement a global tracker for lives and total score.
// 57. [x] **Death/Respawn**: Handle player death and resetting the current screen.
// 58. [x] **HUD**: Create an on-screen display for current score and player lives.
// 
// ## Phase 10: Audio & Polish
// 59. [x] **Sound Engine**: Implement a basic audio manager for SFX.
// 60. [x] **BGM**: Add looping background music tracks for the level.
// 61. [x] **SFX - Movement**: Add sounds for jumping and walking.
// 62. [x] **SFX - Combat**: Add sounds for barrel collisions and rivet removals.
// 63. [x] **SFX - UI**: Add sounds for menu navigation and game over.
// 64. [x] **Visual Polish**: Add screen shake or particle effects for the rivet collapse.
// 65. [x] **Final Balancing**: Tune movement speeds and barrel spawn rates across all 4 screens.
// 66. [x] **End-to-End Test**: Conduct a full playthrough from title screen to the final rivet.

$meta
  title = Donkey Kong (1981) Arcade Recreation
  description = A complete recreation of the 1981 Nintendo arcade classic Donkey Kong — four screens, rolling barrels, fireballs, hammers, rivets, ladders and Pauline's rescue. Built for perchance.org with vanilla JS + canvas.
  tags = arcade, game, platformer, donkey kong, recreation, retro, nintendo
